WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.840
The water fountain down the hall
at school costs you nothing.

2
00:00:03.840 --> 00:00:05.930
Nobody gives it a second thought.

3
00:00:05.930 --> 00:00:07.720
At the jewelry store in the mall,

4
00:00:07.720 --> 00:00:12.000
a diamond smaller than a pea
carries a giant price tag.

5
00:00:12.000 --> 00:00:13.960
But water is vital.

6
00:00:13.960 --> 00:00:16.000
A diamond just sparkles.

7
00:00:16.000 --> 00:00:19.150
Economists call this the paradox of value.

8
00:00:19.150 --> 00:00:21.290
So why does the one you can't live without

9
00:00:21.290 --> 00:00:23.250
cost so much less?

10
00:00:23.250 --> 00:00:26.820
In this mission, you'll calculate
marginal utility per dollar

11
00:00:26.820 --> 00:00:29.720
and find the best way to
spend a limited budget.

12
00:00:29.720 --> 00:00:34.310
Then you'll see why a smart choice
ignores money you've already spent.

13
00:00:34.310 --> 00:00:38.840
Your mission: figure out why diamonds
cost so much more than water.
